<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal CPI index fell 0.1 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>Portugal CPI index fell 0.1 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese consumer prices fell 0.1 percent in October after standing unchanged in September to give year-on-year inflation of 3.0 percent after 3.4 percent in September, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>Average annual inflation, the government's yardstick, was</p>
<p>3.2 percent in October after 3.3 percent percent in September.</p>
<p> PORTUGUESE INFLATION	  Oct 96	 Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI rise		 -0.1	 unch	   0.4</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation		3.0	  3.4	   4.0</p>
<p> Average annual inflation	3.2	  3.3	   4.2</p>
<p> Index (base 100 1991)	 131.9	 132.0	 128.1</p>
<p>    SECTOR			OCT 96	SEPT 96	OCT 95</p>
<p>Food and drink		 -0.8 pct    -0.3 pct     +0.3 pct</p>
<p>Shoes and clothing	   +0.4 pct    +0.3 pct	unch</p>
<p>Household goods		+0.3 pct    +0.3 pct     +0.2 pct</p>
<p>Health			   +0.4 pct    +0.1 pct     +0.3 pct</p>
<p>Transport, communications  +0.3 pct    +0.1 pct     +0.2 pct</p>
<p>Schooling, entertainment   +2.1 pct    +0.2 pct     +2.5 pct</p>
<p>Tobacco			  +0.1 pct    +2.2 pct	unch</p>
<p>Other goods and services   +0.1 pct    +0.5 pct     +0.2 pct</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
